{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:9-7","provision":"BCO 9-7","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"9-7","title":"Section 9-7","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/9-7/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/9-7","current_text":{"html":"<p>It is often expedient that the Session of a church should select and appoint godly men and women of the congregation to assist the deacons in caring for the sick, the widows, the orphans, the prisoners, and others who may be in any distress or need. These assistants to the deacons are not officers of the church (<i>BCO </i>7-2) and, as such, are not subjects for ordination (<i>BCO </i>17).</p>","text":"It is often expedient that the Session of a church should select and appoint godly men and women of the congregation to assist the deacons in caring for the sick, the widows, the orphans, the prisoners, and others who may be in any distress or need. These assistants to the deacons are not officers of the church (BCO 7-2) and, as such, are not subjects for ordination (BCO 17)."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"128cf7cdd1263685b0a4c3f3f98d6149b2d89fd2b9b08848b1b45bbc05a5836d","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":1148