ontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-7--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md:occ-c3f1f581d2c8","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"CCB found an overture appointing unordained persons to diaconal ministry in conflict with the Constitution, including because it implied an unordained office contrary to BCO 17-1.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga38_2010__ci04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null}},{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Brown v. Northern California Presbytery","year":2011,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-6f192cd8033c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":215},"excerpt":"As specifically described, there is nothing in the Constitution that prohibits the practice of this view. It matches closely the provision of BCO 9-7:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-dd6e852d316e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":263},"excerpt":"It should be noted the Complainants rightly point to a potential problem. BCO 9-7 describes the appointment of both women and men to assist the Deacons. If male assistants are thus appointed, it is unclear what title would be given to them, and this could be…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-b8ed529c0172","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":269},"excerpt":"…Congregational election instead of Session appointment, which is authorized by BCO 9-7, to pick or select diaconal assistants fails the “distinctive means” standard of Kniseley and therefore is not “wise, equitable or suited to promote the welfare of the…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-12df3bc10b88","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":303},"excerpt":"…be permissible to say the Diaconal Assistants appointed by the Session, per BCO 9-7, serve as \"equal partners\" with the Deacons in accomplishing these ministries.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-6303a7d0162b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":349},"excerpt":"…or as a Deacon. Presumably, they would simply be appointed by the Session (BCO 9-7), similar to other volunteers and even paid staff. Also, under the NORD view, no one is allowed to vote or serve as chairman or secretary, since only men ordained to the…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"},{"id":"bco:9-7--case:cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md:occ-c6c91ce5b8ef","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.html","repository_path":"cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":382},"excerpt":"…only ordained and elected men can be Members of a “diaconate.\" The appeal to BCO 9-7 is flawed because 9- 7 addresses people appointed by the Session, not Members of a Diaconate (Board of Deacons, 9-4). According to BCO 9-3 and 9-4, a Diaconate may only…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga39_2011__2009-25_2009-26.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["diaconate","deaconess","women in church office","in thesi statement","abstract decree","presbyterial jurisdiction","BCO 9-7","appointed deaconess","elected deaconess","equal partners","nobody ordained","GUMP standard","Kniseley standard"],"standard_of_review":"